unctate keratitis","hpo_label":"Punctate keratitis","hpo_id":"HP:0011859","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"reduced tear film break-up time","hpo_label":"Brief tear break-up time","hpo_id":"HP:6000069","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"oligodontia with persisting deciduous teeth and only two permanent teeth","hpo_label":"Oligodontia","hpo_id":"HP:0000677","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"persistence of primary teeth","hpo_label":"Persistence of primary teeth","hpo_id":"HP:0006335","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"delayed tooth eruption","hpo_label":"Delayed eruption of teeth","hpo_id":"HP:0000684","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"absent sweat glands on skin biopsy","hpo_label":"Aplasia of the sweat glands","hpo_id":"HP:0011136","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"focal subcorneal clefting and basal spongiosis","hpo_label":"Spongiosis","hpo_id":"HP:6001166","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"natal teeth","hpo_label":"Natal tooth","hpo_id":"HP:0000695","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"normal scalp hair, eyebrows and eyelashes","hpo_label":"Sparse scalp hair","hpo_id":"HP:0002209","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"syndactyly","hpo_label":"Syndactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0001159","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"normal breasts and nipples","hpo_label":"Hypoplastic nipples","hpo_id":"HP:0002557","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"lip and palate abnormality","hpo_label":"Cleft lip","hpo_id":"HP:0410030","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"IRF6","as_reported":"c.658 T>C (p.Ser220Pro)","cdna":"c.658T>C","protein":"p.Ser220Pro","genomic":"","zygosity":"mosaic","origin":"de_novo","consequence":"missense","key":"V3"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"de novo; mosaic (VAF 30.5%); trio WGS with healthy non-consanguineous parents","inheritance":"SOMATIC_MOSAIC","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["In patient 3 (P3), a 22‐year‐old woman referred for anhidrosis, dry skin and intolerance to environmental temperatures above 22°C, diffuse xerosis and dilatation of the follicular ostia were noted.","identified a heterozygous de novo IRF6 variant, c.658 T>C (p.Ser220Pro), with a variant allele frequency of 30.5% (T: 42 | C: 18) indicating mosaicism.","Interestingly, patient 3 presented with 16 persisting deciduous teeth and only two permanent teeth after delayed tooth eruption."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"SOMATIC_MOSAIC","genotype_reason":"stated for the family"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:42487474:1","pmid":"42487474","section":"nomenclature","statement":"Schneider et al. (2026) noted that they had initially referred to this IRF6-associated ectodermal dysplasia as ectodermal dysplasia with natal teeth (EDNAT), but because natal teeth were absent in 3 of 5 known patients, they concluded that natal teeth are not as typical as initially thought.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["We initially referred to this new disease as Ectodermal Dysplasia with Natal Teeth (EDNAT)","However, the two Asian patients, P4 and P5, also did not show natal teeth (Dr. Zhimiao Lin, personal communication), indicating that they are not as typical as initially thought."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:42487474:2","pmid":"42487474","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Schneider et al. (2026) considered a combination of oligodontia, hypo- or anhidrosis, hidradenitis suppurativa-like skin abscesses, poikiloderma, onychodysplasia, and bilateral hearing impairment to be syndrome-defining for IRF6-associated ectodermal dysplasia, while natal teeth and sparse hair were irregular or variable; lip pits and cleft lip/palate were absent in all 5 known patients.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["A combination of oligodontia, hypo‐ or anhidrosis, hidradenitis suppurativa‐like skin abscesses, poikiloderma, onychodysplasia and bilateral hearing impairment is considered to be syndrome‐defining, while natal teeth and sparse hair were observed irregularly or may be variable."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:42487474:3","pmid":"42487474","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Schneider et al. (2026) recognized a common pattern of tooth agenesis in 3 unrelated patients: all had permanent upper incisors but lacked mandibular incisors and canines and all permanent premolars, with pronounced atrophy of the lower alveolar crest.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["All three patients had permanent incisors in the upper jaw, but no incisors or canines in the mandible, and none of these unrelated individuals had any permanent premolars (Figure 4)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:42487474:4","pmid":"42487474","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Schneider et al. (2026) found by immunofluorescence that keratinocyte nuclei from a patient with IRF6 Ile218Asn showed stronger IRF6 staining than controls, whereas the mosaic Ser220Pro patient showed patchy nuclear staining; keratin-17 staining was normal. Together with genotype-phenotype correlations, they suggested a gain-of-function mechanism.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["The nuclei of keratinocytes from P1 showed stronger specific staining (Figure 2E,F) than control nuclei (Figure 2A,B), while an apparently more patchy nuclear staining was observed in the epidermis of P3 (Figure 2G,H), fitting with genetic mosaicism.","Genotype‐phenotype correlations from a total of five patients and immunohistochemical data support the assumption that IRF6‐associated ED is based on a gain‐of‐function mechanism."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:42487474:5","pmid":"42487474","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Schneider et al. (2026) noted that the ED-associated substitutions in exon 6 of IRF6 lie in a region between the DNA-binding and protein-binding domains with no assigned function, and AlphaFold3 modeling placed both point mutations in a short alpha-helix at the end of this region, predicted with higher confidence than the rest of the region.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["However, the point mutations causing the new disease entity both affect a short alpha‐helix at the end of this region, predicted with a considerably higher confidence value (mostly above 70)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:41046129:1","pmid":"41046129","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Zhang et al. (2026) reported that gain-of-function variants in IRF6 cause a syndrome of hidradenitis suppurativa, ectodermal dysplasia, and deafness.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Gain-of-function variants in IRF6 cause hidradenitis suppurativa, ectodermal dysplasia and deafness syndrome."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:39902929:1","pmid":"39902929","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Peschel et al. (2025) reported a previously undescribed variant in the IRF6 gene that they concluded caused a new type of ectodermal dysplasia with natal teeth.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["A yet undescribed IRF6 variant causes a new type of ectodermal dysplasia with natal teeth."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["IRF6"],"confirmed":["IRF6"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AD"]}